ficient to overcome absence of chronic features."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute pain progression over days reduce the likelihood of adnexal torsion compared to acute hemodynamic presentations?", "summary": "Subacute pain progression weakly contradicts adnexal torsion (B1.1), but the sudden exacerbation during exercise preserves it as a consideration."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's athletic build and recent weight loss (for fitness competition) contradict the typical presentation of ectopic pregnancy with hemorrhage?", "summary": "Intentional weight loss for a fitness competition strongly contradicts ectopic pregnancy with hemorrhage (B1.2), as extreme weight loss is uncommon in this condition."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of known chronic liver disease risk factors (e.g., cirrhosis) in the vignette rule out Budd-Chiari syndrome as a likely diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of chronic liver disease risk factors weakly reduces Budd-Chiari syndrome (B2.1) likelihood, but acute presentations can occur without prior risk factors."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's hypotension and tachycardia support acute hepatic vascular pathology as the cause of haemodynamic instability?", "summary": "The presence of hypotension and tachycardia provides moderate support for hepatic vascular pathology (B2) and other acute abdominal emergencies (B5). These findings are less specific for gynecological (B1), biliary (B3), or pancreatic (B4) causes."}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Patient is hypotensive (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm) indicating major haemodynamic instability. Severe right upper quadrant pain raises concern for acute abdomen with potential systemic complications.", "required_actions": ["Initiate vasopressor support for hypotension", "Order urgent imaging (e.g., ultrasound/CT) to evaluate liver and biliary structures", "Administer broad-spectrum antibiotics for possible septic shock until labs confirm or rule out infection"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "[static mode override] Patient is hypotensive (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm) indicating major haemodynamic instability requiring urgent intervention. Severe right upper quadrant pain raises concern for acute abdomen with potential systemic complications. — emergency_override suppressed in static_diagnosis_qa mode"}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.82, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.05981825883773298, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Arterial hypotension', 'Acute pancreatitis', 'Liver disease', 'Chronic pancreatitis', 'Postural hypotension with compensatory tachycardia', 'Budd-Chiari syndrome'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.429}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B5", "label": "Other Acute Abdominal Emergencies", "posterior": 0.06, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broade